[size=5][b]Update game DLLs and inspect driver updates from one Windows app.[/b][/size]

DLSSync updates supported DLSS, FSR, XeSS, Streamline and DirectStorage DLLs already present in game folders. It also offers GPU and Windows device-driver workflows. Local DLL snapshots and an operation journal help you inspect changes and restore retained backups.

[url=https://github.com/xt0n1-t3ch/DLSSync][img]https://img.shields.io/badge/Source-Code_on_GitHub-181717?style=for-the-badge&logo=github&logoColor=white[/img][/url]
[url=https://github.com/xt0n1-t3ch/DLSSync-Manifest][img]https://img.shields.io/badge/Signed-Public_Catalog-0B8F6A?style=for-the-badge&logo=files&logoColor=white[/img][/url][/center]

[size=4][b]What the app manages[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]NVIDIA:[/b] DLSS Super Resolution, Frame Generation, Ray Reconstruction, Streamline and Reflex files.
[*][b]AMD:[/b] Recognized FidelityFX upscaler, frame-generation, loader, Vulkan and denoiser runtimes.
[*][b]Intel:[/b] XeSS Super Resolution, XeSS Frame Generation and XeLL.
[*][b]Microsoft:[/b] DirectStorage and DirectStorage Core.
[*][b]Drivers:[/b] NVIDIA, AMD and Intel GPU package workflows plus applicable Windows device-driver updates.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Understand the checks and limits[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Catalog metadata has a detached Ed25519 signature. Artifact hashes use each entry's recorded algorithm, including SHA-256 and historical MD5. Publisher verification is a separate Authenticode check.
[*]Sources include first-party releases and labeled DLSS Swapper community-archive history. An original vendor signature does not make an archive first-party.
[*]Backups use SHA-256 to validate local snapshot bytes. Missing snapshots, locks, permissions and validation failures can prevent restore.
[*]A correct hash does not prove that a game, GPU or mod combination works. Updating DLLs does not add a missing game integration.
[*]Check a protected game's policy before changing files or driver profiles. An absent warning is not permission to modify it.
[*]GPU installer outcomes and Windows driver recovery are separate from game DLL backups. A System Restore checkpoint is not guaranteed.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Required NexusBuild- behavior[/b][/size]

The Nexus channel must have [b]no app self-updater and no automatic app-update or catalog network calls[/b]. Catalog refresh and every other network action must be [b]explicit and manual[/b]. Opening a page is not consent to a network lookup.

The embedded signed catalog supports the initial offline state. [b]Refresh Catalog[/b] explicitly retrieves current metadata and its detached signature for validation. Install future app versions manually from Nexus Mods.

Standard and Nexus use the same source commit and one [b]v1.7.0[/b] tag. Nexus assets use distinct [b]NexusBuild-[/b] names. Standard's updater feed points only to the exact Standard installer and carries its matching signature. The public release assets, SHA-256 inventory and updater feed were verified on September 20, 2026. A separate packaged network capture is still required before making a broader claim about every possible third-party request.

[size=4][b]Use DLSSync[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install or extract the intended channel and open [b]Library[/b].
[*]Scan supported launchers or add the actual game folder through Settings. Discovery is not exhaustive.
[*]Close the game and inspect detected components, versions and warnings.
[*]Use the game's one-click update action. Routine updates prepare internally without a separate confirmation; validation can still reject an operation.
[*]Read the per-file result and test the game. Use [b]Backups[/b] to restore retained snapshots if needed.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Privacy and requirements[/b][/size]

Windows 10/11 x64 with WebView2. Game-folder writes, driver operations and some installation formats can require additional permissions. The repository has no telemetry endpoint, but functional network requests can send game titles or device compatibility parameters. Optional SteamGridDB lookup uses bearer authentication. Opening a prefilled GitHub issue URL sends its report contents before issue submission; review and redact diagnostics first.

Portable mode uses data beside the executable when portable.flag is present and disables app self-update. Keep its backups and operation journal when moving the app.

